{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522567-werewolves-seeing-through-obfuscate-in-vda20-and-wta20-a-new-perspective","id":1522567,"title":"Werewolves seeing through Obfuscate in VDA20 and WTA20: a new perspective","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-14T07:15:27-07:00","id":1522567,"title":"Werewolves seeing through Obfuscate in VDA20 and WTA20: a new perspective","content":"Hi! I know this issue has come up in other threads, with one of the most frequent answers being that there is no set system to determine whether werewolves can see through Obfuscate, but generally one compares the werewolf's rank (as if it was Auspex) with the vampire's Obfuscate rating <i>if</i> the werewolf has a gift to see through supernatural concealment. This is the take that most stayed in my memory, though others were offered.<br /> <br /> Now, here's my problem: we are playing VDA20, but using WTA20 for werewolves rules. We are not using other supplements from either line. I went through the gifts in WTA's core manual and... I can't find any that would make me say: this would apply to Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Those that I recall now:<br /> Sense the Wyrm: first, this seems to give vague impressions about the presence of Wyrm taint, not to pinpoint the location of a vampire. Second, Unseen Presence (Obfuscate 2) works by making others <i>unconsciously</i> oblivious to the vampire's presence unless s/he draws attention to himself or herself by affecting other things. It's so deep that people unconsciously move aside to make the vampire pass. The vampire is not actually invisible, but is rather ignored. I don't see why even a lupine sensing the Wyrm should not unconsciously ignore the vampire, even though technically he senses his Wyrm taint. As for Vanish from the Mind's Eye, that explicitly fools all senses, so I don't see why a sense like the Wyrm-sense should not be fooled as well. Nothing in the description of Sense the Wyrm says that it pierces supernatural concealment.<br /> <br /> Sense the Unnatural: this has the same issue as Sense the Wyrm. It does not, in principle, pierce supernatural concealment, and even if the lupine senses a vampire is near, he would be brought to ignore that sensation by Obfuscate's mind influence.<br /> <br /> Scent something (can't recall the proper name): a power that lets you swap.your sight for your smell to smell invisible entities. Again: Unseen Presence doesn't actually make you invisible, it makes you ignored, so I don't see why using smell would pierce it. Your nose smells the vampire, but your mind ignores that input. And as for Vanish from the Mind's Eye, it explicitly tricks all senses, so smell offer no special help against it. This scent power seems great to fight spirits or some type of mages maybe (not sure) or those who use magical invisibility rather than the mind-influence of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Which other powers am I forgetting? Am I reading this wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T07:35:42-07:00","id":1522568,"title":"","content":"What you say makes complete sense. Enhanced senses shouldn't help with Obfuscate because it's not that you can't sense them already, you do, its just that your mind wont recognize that you see them. Then again, by that logic Auspex shouldn't help with Obfuscate either but it explicitly says that it helps.<br /> <br /> To follow this line of thinking, sensory powers shouldn't necessarily help werewolves see through Obfuscate, but any Gift or ability that gives the werewolf immunity or resistance to mind control should protect them from Obfuscate. Like Mindblock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T07:45:16-07:00","id":1522571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522567-werewolves-seeing-through-obfuscate-in-vda20-and-wta20-a-new-perspective?p=1522568#post1522568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you say makes complete sense. Enhanced senses shouldn't help with Obfuscate because it's not that you can't sense them already, you do, its just that your mind wont recognize that you see them. Then again, by that logic Auspex shouldn't help with Obfuscate either but it explicitly says that it helps.<br /> <br /> To follow this line of thinking, sensory powers shouldn't necessarily help werewolves see through Obfuscate, but any Gift or ability that gives the werewolf immunity or resistance to mind control should protect them from Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Indeed, resistance to mind control would be the key here. Might need to re-read the list of gifts to see which ones offer that. In fact, in VDA20, 3 dots in True Faith (or maybe 2) protect from mental manipulation, and Obfuscate is explicitly listed there along with Dominate.<br /> <br /> As for Auspex, I agree it is weird, but I think the deal with it is that Auspex by itself, regardless of its specific powers, pierces through mental illusions as well as illusions of the senses, yet it does not pierce through metaphyisical or mystical veils (ex: it doesn't let you see spirits or ghosts beyond the Gauntlet / Shroud). And in fact, all Auspex powers from 2 to 5 concern the mind in some way: sense emotions through auras, though also see the supernatural nature of those around you; sense psychic residues on touched objects; read people's minds and send thoughts into them; project your mind to perceive far away things (this is no more proper astral travel in VDA20, but just a projection of your consciousness elsewhere in the physical world). So it kind of makes sense that Auspex in some way protects from mental illusions. At lease to my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T08:01:24-07:00","id":1522572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">World of Darkness really needed something like the Clash of Wills system. I can't really remember a time where these things weren't awkward to adjudicate in an edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that. It is a bit annoying to have so many things that have to be sorted out between Narrators and players because the rules leave weird gaps.<br /> <br /> I am totally fine with the idea of vampires having special invisibility powers that werewolves struggle to break, and since vampires are a low-ranking concern for werewolves and not every clan has Obfuscate, it makes sense lupines would not develop gifts to counter it. In fact, since vampires typically are weaker than werewolves until they become elders, it makes perfect evolutionary sense that they would have a discipline that shields them well from lupines, while lupines develop few tools to deal with vampires since they already have the advantage over them.<br /> Nonetheless, it would be better if this fact was stated explicitly in the manuals, since it's an obvious question people would ask (how do their common powers interact?), instead of needing to be figured out through careful research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T10:10:06-07:00","id":1522580,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of different interpretations about a number of powers when it comes it werewolves vs vampires. I\u2019ve seen some people basically interpret things to make werewolves nearly immune to all vampire powers - like letting any werewolf have a chance at resisting Obfuscate because they have wolf senses.<br /> <br /> I tend to lean in the other direction, if there is doubt or ambiguity, I think it\u2019s better to error on the vampire\u2019s side since werewolves already have so many advantages. Of course, each Storyteller should rule as he or she feels is appropriate for the chronicle.<br /> <br /> In this case, I think it\u2019s not unreasonable to require some kind of mental defense for a werewolf to resist Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T12:59:28-07:00","id":1522591,"title":"","content":"I think you can skip a lot of the uncertainty around specific Gifts if you remember that piercing Obfuscate isn't automatic, it's a roll-off. Having an appropriate power is a prerequisite to getting to make the roll, not automatic sensing the vampire. It's not like Auspex 1's specific mechanics are protecting you from mental influence in general, it just contests Chimerstry and Obfuscate because the game needed some counter to them.<br /> <br /> Garou Gifts aren't organized into neat packages like Disciplines where you can just say, &quot;having anything is this package counts as being able to counter Obfuscate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given how the rolls work, there really isn't a serious danger with being liberal in interpreting Garou Gifts as qualifying. A fresh Cliath isn't detecting an Elder Nosferatu just because they have Sense Wyrm. If you want some middle ground, just have it be the Rank of the Gift not the Rank of the Garou that dictates the mechanics of the roll off. A level 1 Garou Gift even in the hands of an Elder werewolf isn't going to be as good as a level 3 Gift.<br /> <br /> Forcing Garou to have a mental-defense Gift isn't in-line with how the VtM rules are actually phrased: &quot;Auspex enables Kindred to perceive many things beyond the limits of lesser senses.<br /> \u200bAmong its many uses, Auspex can detect the presence of a supernatural being who is hidden from normal sight (a vampire using Obfuscate, for example, or a ghost) or pierce illusions created by the Discipline of Chimerstry.&quot; It doesn't say that this works because Auspex is actually a mental defense power, it says it works because supernatural perception powers can overcome mental deceptions.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T14:29:53-07:00","id":1522599,"title":"","content":"I deleted the reply to Heavy Arms because I was tired when I wrote it, then I reread his message and thought I probably missed his point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":".  I deleted the reply to Heavy Arms because I was tired when I wrote it, then I reread his message and thought I probably missed his point 09-14-2023, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T15:22:42-07:00","id":1522604,"title":"","content":"You might find this <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512221-werewols-countering-obfuscate-and-presence\">thread on the Werewolf forum</a> useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T15:59:08-07:00","id":1522607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">World of Darkness really needed something like the Clash of Wills system. I can't really remember a time where these things weren't awkward to adjudicate in an edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the suggested crossover rules for W:tA in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook actually set things up that way. It's just that V:tM is really dumb and their STH usually insists on &quot;highest level wins&quot; regardless of context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T17:21:39-07:00","id":1522617,"title":"","content":"For the record, I just saw the third level Metis Gift &quot;Shell&quot; (WTA20, p.157) which gives full immunity from &quot;mind-altering magic of all kinds&quot; for one scene. That would work against Obfuscate in my understanding, as well as Dominate and Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T17:43:05-07:00","id":1522618,"title":"","content":"From the wording of the power, I could see Shell making a werewolf completely immune to Obfuscate, even that of a Methuselah. Should the Garou have to compare Rank vs Obfuscate levels when the Gift forces the werewolf to give up Rage use for complete mental immunity?<br /> <br /> if I were the ST I would probably allow the Shell user to have complete immunity to Obfuscate without any roll or comparison needed unless the Obfuscate user was really powerful, like 6+ levels.<br /> <br /> For other Gifts I might decide on a case by case basis whether it\u2019s useless, requires sone roll or comparison, or in rare cases like Shell works automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T23:29:38-07:00","id":1522621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522567-werewolves-seeing-through-obfuscate-in-vda20-and-wta20-a-new-perspective?p=1522618#post1522618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the wording of the power, I could see Shell making a werewolf completely immune to Obfuscate, even that of a Methuselah. Should the Garou have to compare Rank vs Obfuscate levels when the Gift forces the werewolf to give up Rage use for complete mental immunity?<br /> <br /> if I were the ST I would probably allow the Shell user to have complete immunity to Obfuscate without any roll or comparison needed unless the Obfuscate user was really powerful, like 6+ levels.<br /> <br /> For other Gifts I might decide on a case by case basis whether it\u2019s useless, requires sone roll or comparison, or in rare cases like Shell works automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read it, as an ST I would grant complete immunity regardless of power level. It's what the wording says to me, plus giving up Rage is quite a sacrifice, especially if having to confront a vampire, and especially if it's an elder. And its need to be activated makes it already less useful against surprise attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T00:56:09-07:00","id":1522623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522567-werewolves-seeing-through-obfuscate-in-vda20-and-wta20-a-new-perspective?p=1522607#post1522607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the suggested crossover rules for W:tA in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook actually set things up that way. It's just that V:tM is really dumb and their STH usually insists on &quot;highest level wins&quot; regardless of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember. Vampires rule, Werewolves drool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T15:20:03-07:00","id":1522643,"title":"","content":"I'm not overly knowledgeable about how Werewolf powers work, but maybe a willpower &amp; resolve roll might be a good starting point for the Lupine trying to locate a Kindred using Obfuscate with increasing levels of difficulty as the Discipline main deal is keeping you hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T02:34:19-07:00","id":1522951,"title":"","content":"According the W20 a gift isn't even necessary to detect a vampire with obfuscate, a roll of Perception + Primal urge at difficulty 8 allow them to detect supernaturally hidden things/beings with their sense of smell (W20 p.273, there is a table that specifies this) and in Lupus form that difficulty is reduced by 2 thank to the wolf senses. But as said earlier it's still is a contested roll, not an automatic ability","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T19:52:46-07:00","id":1522987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522567-werewolves-seeing-through-obfuscate-in-vda20-and-wta20-a-new-perspective?p=1522951#post1522951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According the W20 a gift isn't even necessary to detect a vampire with obfuscate, a roll of Perception + Primal urge at difficulty 8 allow them to detect supernaturally hidden things/beings with their sense of smell (W20 p.273, there is a table that specifies this) and in Lupus form that difficulty is reduced by 2 thank to the wolf senses. But as said earlier it's still is a contested roll, not an automatic ability</div> </div> </div> </div>You are very right sir!! \u0130 had totally missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T12:20:06-07:00","id":1523043,"title":"","content":"Lines up rather nicely with ghosts and Hungry Dead just being able to do it, too (Lifesight and Deathsight).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}